  Note [status: not-installed]: codex-plugin-cc is not available, so this review ran without an additional Codex review.
  Install it for an extra review gate:
  /plugin marketplace add openai/codex-plugin-cc
  /plugin install codex@openai-codex
  /reload-plugins
  /codex:setup

  My own self-review caught and fixed two things: the constraints section claimed late reminders are "flagged as late"
  when no such field exists (they arrive as [38;5;153moverdue[39m instead), and "fired keys are persisted alongside notifications"
  didn't say where — they live inside the [38;5;153mnotifications.v1[39m record and survive dismissal and the 100-entry trim, which
  matters, since losing them would re-fire old reminders.

  Two things in the spec worth your attention specifically:

  - [1mThe closed-tab ceiling[0m is recorded as a constraint, not a limitation to work around. If it turns out you actually
    need a reminder at 15:00 rather than whenever the page next opens, that's not a bug to fix — it's the signal the
    client-only decision needs revisiting.
  - [1mDeclining Playwright leaves the riskiest paths uncovered[0m — permission prompts, visibility routing, reload
    persistence. That's recorded under Accepted Risks with manual verification as the mitigation, rather than quietly
    omitted.

  Please review the spec and let me know if you want changes before I write the implementation plan.

